  "worked_solution": "Let's denote:\n\n- $P(n):\\,\\sqrt{n}\\notin N$\n\n- $Q(n):\\,n\u22232$\n\nThen, our statement can be written as\n\n$$\n\u2203n\\,P(n)\u21d2\u2200n\\,Q(n).\n$$\n\nBy eliminating implication, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2203n\\,P(n)\u21d2\u2200n\\,Q(n) & \u2261\u00ac(\u2203n\\,P(n))\u2228\u2200n\\,Q(n) \\\\  & \u2261\u2200n\\,\u00acP(n)\u2228\u2200n\\,Q(n)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can't \"factor out\" the quantifier since, in general, \n\n$$\n\u2200n\\,P(n)\u2228\u2200n\\,Q(n)\u2262\u2200n\\,(P(n)\u2228Q(n)).\n$$\n\nHowever, we can change the variable in one of the predicates. For example, in the second one:\n\n$$\n\u2200n\\,P(n)\u2228\u2200n\\,Q(n)\u2261\u2200n\\,P(n)\u2228\u2200m\\,Q(m)\n$$\n\nNow, since $P(n)$ does not depend on $m$ and $Q(m)$ does not depend on $n,$ we can move the quantifiers to the front, as follows:\n\n$$\n\u2200n\\,\u00acP(n)\u2228\u2200m\\,Q(m)\u2261\u2200n\\,\u2200m\\,(\u00acP(n)\u2228Q(m))\n$$\n\nThe final expression reads \n\n$\\,$ $\u2200n,m\\in N\\,(\\sqrt{n}\\in N\u2228m\u22232).$",
